  "react_vs_plan": "ReAct makes one model decision per observation, so the measured S1/S5/S6 calls are 5/3/2 and each decision can adapt to NOT_FOUND or a cancelled order. A plan-and-execute design could reduce normal model calls by requesting the whole sequence once, but it must replan when a tool returns an unexpected result and risks executing a stale plan. For this refund workflow I prefer ReAct because correctness and safe stopping matter more than saving a few local mock calls; every refund decision is checked against the database and policy before money is issued."
